    "result_text": "Tests are green. I agreed with the finding and addressed it.\n\n**What I changed:**\n\n- Added a new `CityCapacity` helper (mirroring the existing `BusinessDay` idiom) as the single source of truth for the per-city rule: `countOwnersIn(city, repository)` plus the `CAPACITY = 50` and `WARNING_THRESHOLD = 40` constants.\n- `CheckOwnerCityCapacity` (hard cap) now calls `CityCapacity.countOwnersIn(...)` and compares against `CityCapacity.CAPACITY`, dropping its inlined stream and its private `CITY_CAPACITY` constant (and the now-unused `Owner` import).\n- `AssignCityCapacityWarning` (warning flag) collapses to the same shape as its day-based sibling `AssignBulkSignupWarning`: fetch the shared count, compare against the shared thresholds. Its Javadoc now points at the shared helper as the enforced invariant instead of asserting the match in prose.\n\nThe duplicated city-counting stream and the duplicated `50` constant are both gone, so the cap and the warning can no longer drift. All acceptance behaviour is unchanged and the full suite passes.",
